1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:22,900
Next is the Monitoring Sheet, the curriculum grid the Graduate School used to keep in Excel: one row per student, one column per subject. In the portal, Graduate School staff keep it current on the screen, and every entry records its source.

2
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:31,300
Graduate School staff signs in.

3
00:00:34,600 --> 00:01:01,799
This is the Monitoring Sheet, under Records. Graduate School staff picks the Master of Science in Nursing program. Each row is a student, each column a subject. The colour shows completed, enrolled, or not yet taken, and the legend explains every mark. Staff can still upload a workbook under Student Handoff instead.

4
00:01:02,799 --> 00:01:17,000
Adding a student missing from the imported sheet. The window says up front: this is a manual entry, recorded with the staff member's name and time.

5
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:39,399
Graduate School staff types the student ID, name, and school year of entry. The import's required fields and duplicate checks apply here too, so manual entries are no sloppier than imports.

6
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:51,599
The student is added, with a Student Portal login, exactly like an import. Graduate School staff adds the subjects next.

7
00:01:52,599 --> 00:02:03,700
This is the student's record panel: all eighteen subjects of the curriculum, none taken yet, with the units counted automatically.

8
00:02:08,699 --> 00:02:19,600
Graduate School staff adds a subject: status Completed, the term, and a remark, here 'credited from a transfer record'.

9
00:02:25,699 --> 00:02:40,300
After the second subject: two of eighteen completed, six units. In the Source column both rows say Manual entry, so nobody mistakes manual data for imported data.

10
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:56,300
To correct a remark, Graduate School staff edits the row. A portal entry needs only a simple edit.

11
00:03:00,099 --> 00:03:15,500
Removing a row needs a reason. The row is not erased: it returns to not taken and stays in the history.

12
00:03:15,699 --> 00:03:20,400
One completed subject remains. The counts update.

13
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:40,400
This is the Change history tab. Every add, change and removal appears with old value, new value, who made it, when, source, and reason. That is the audit trail.

14
00:03:42,199 --> 00:03:56,000
Back on the grid, the new student carries a Manual tag. The hand-entered cell has a small orange dot, so manual data shows at a glance.

15
00:03:57,099 --> 00:04:06,500
Now an imported student, Katrina Cabrera. Every row says Imported: official workbook values.

16
00:04:06,699 --> 00:04:28,100
Changing an imported value requires a reason before the system saves it, and the history records the reason with the staff member's name. Official values are never overwritten silently. Grades are never entered here: AIMS is the official source.
